  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1203.28 Magnetic wire insulation coating",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1203.28 \"Magnetic wire insulation coating\" means a coating in which an electrically-insulated varnish or enamel is applied onto the surface of wire for use in electrical machinery.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
